---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const REPO = "https://github.com/Aliserag/Rancor";
import themes from "../data/themes_islamophobia.json";
const kwLists = (themes as any).keywords.lists;
const kwCount = kwLists.reduce((n: number, l: any) => n + l.terms.length, 0);
const fwItemCount = (themes as any).frameworks.reduce((n: number, f: any) => n + f.items.length, 0);
---

<Base
  title="Developers"
  active="mcp"
  description="Run Rancor's instrument against your own model as an MCP server: list cited anti-Muslim narrative themes and keyword lists, score responses with the same three-judge panel, and gate a release on the result."
  heading="Test your model before it ships">
  <h2>Test your model before it ships</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/">The leaderboard</a> tells you how models that already shipped handle
    anti-Muslim bias. The same instrument plugs into your editor or agent as
    an MCP server, so a team building a model can test it before release, not
    after. MCP, the Model Context Protocol, is an open standard that lets AI
    tools call other tools.
  </p>

  <h3>Quickstart</h3>
  <p>From a clone of the repository:</p>
  <pre><code>python -m rancor.mcp_server</code></pre>
  <p>
    Or point any MCP client at the config shipped at the repository root
    (<code>mcp.json</code>):
  </p>
  <pre
    is:raw><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "rancor": {
      "command": "./.venv/bin/python",
      "args": [
        "-m",
        "rancor.mcp_server"
      ],
      "env": {
        "OPENROUTER_API_KEY": "${OPENROUTER_API_KEY}"
      }
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
  <p class="note">
    <code>describe_instrument</code>, <code>list_prompts</code> and
    <code>list_themes</code> work offline. Only the tools that call models
    need an <code>OPENROUTER_API_KEY</code>. Measured against production,
    scoring one prompt end to end costs about 0.039 OpenRouter credits.
  </p>

  <h3>The six tools</h3>
  <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Tool reference, scrollable">
    <table class="ledger">
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><code>describe_instrument</code></th>
          <td>What Rancor measures: axes, categories, prompt-set hash, judge panel.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><code>list_prompts</code></th>
          <td>Browse the frozen prompt set, filtered by axis, category or a text query.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><code>list_themes</code></th>
          <td>Cited reference of documented hate-narrative themes and keyword lists for an axis, for writing your own test prompts and lexical screens.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><code>probe_models</code></th>
          <td>Run one prompt across the pinned model panel, or against any single OpenRouter model.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><code>score_response</code></th>
          <td>Score one response with the fixed three-judge panel against the published rubric for that axis and category.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><code>evaluate_model</code></th>
          <td>Pre-ship gate: run a candidate model against curated items, score every answer, return per-item scores and the mean.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>The loop for developers</h3>
  <p>
    <code>list_themes</code> gives you a cited map of documented anti-Muslim
    narrative themes and keyword lists, explorable below.
    Write your own test prompts against each theme
    that matters for your product. <code>score_response</code> grades every
    answer with the same fixed three-judge panel and published rubric the
    leaderboard uses. <code>evaluate_model</code> then works as a pre-ship
    gate: a build can fail on a regression.
  </p>

  <h3>What these scores are</h3>
  <p>
    Scores from these tools are diagnostics. Published leaderboard figures
    come only from graded runs with a manifest, and
    <code>describe_instrument</code> says exactly that in its own output.
  </p>


  <h3 id="theme-map">The theme map, explorable</h3>
  <p class="note">
    The exact data <code>list_themes</code> serves: {(themes as any).frameworks.length} published
    frameworks ({fwItemCount} items), {(themes as any).themes.length} contemporary narrative
    themes distilled from GNCI research, and {kwCount} keywords and coded
    catchphrases. Every entry cited.
  </p>

  <div class="fw-row">
    {(themes as any).frameworks.map((fw: any, i: number) => (
      <details class="fw" open={i === 0}>
        <summary>{fw.name} <span class="pill">{fw.items.length}</span></summary>
        <ul>
          {fw.items.map((it: any) => (
            <li><strong>{it.name}.</strong> {it.description}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="cites">
          {fw.sources.map((src: any) => (
            <a href={src.url}>{src.cite.split(";")[0]}</a>
          ))}
        </p>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p class="theme-toolbar">
    <input id="theme-search" type="search" placeholder="Filter the 32 themes: replacement, taqiyya, refugees…" aria-label="Filter themes" />
    <span id="theme-count" class="note" aria-live="polite"></span>
  </p>
  <div id="theme-grid">
    {(themes as any).themes.map((t: any) => (
      <article class="theme-card">
        <h4>{t.name}</h4>
        <p>{t.description}</p>
        <p class="cites">{t.sources.map((src: any) => `${src.doc}, p. ${src.pages}`).join(" · ")}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="note">{(themes as any).source_note}</p>

  <h3>Keyword lists for lexical screening</h3>
  {kwLists.map((l: any) => (
    <details class="kw">
      <summary>{l.name} <span class="pill">{l.terms.length}</span></summary>
      {l.note && <p class="note">{l.note}</p>}
      <p class="chips">
        {l.terms.map((t: any) => (
          <span class="chip">{typeof t === "string" ? t : t.term}</span>
        ))}
      </p>
      {l.sources && (
        <p class="cites">
          {l.sources.map((src: any) => <a href={src.url}>{src.cite.split(",")[0]}</a>)}
        </p>
      )}
    </details>
  ))}
  <p class="note">{(themes as any).keywords.about}</p>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      const input = document.getElementById("theme-search");
      const count = document.getElementById("theme-count");
      const cards = [...document.querySelectorAll(".theme-card")];
      const update = () => {
        const q = input.value.trim().toLowerCase();
        let shown = 0;
        for (const c of cards) {
          const hit = !q || c.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(q);
          c.hidden = !hit;
          if (hit) shown++;
        }
        count.textContent = q ? `${shown} of ${cards.length} themes` : "";
      };
      input.addEventListener("input", update);
    })();
  </script>

  <style>
    .fw-row { display: grid; gap: 0.6rem; margin: 0 0 1.4rem; }
    details.fw, details.kw {
      border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent, #9c2b2b);
      background: var(--panel); padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem; border-radius: 4px;
    }
    details.fw summary, details.kw summary {
      cursor: pointer; font-weight: 700; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.85rem;
    }
    .pill {
      font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--paper);
      background: var(--ink); border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.05rem 0.5rem; margin-left: 0.3rem;
    }
    .theme-toolbar { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.8rem; margin: 0 0 0.8rem; }
    #theme-search {
      flex: 1; max-width: 26rem; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.85rem;
      padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--panel);
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    #theme-grid {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(17rem, 1fr));
      gap: 0.7rem; margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    }
    .theme-card {
      border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--panel); border-radius: 4px;
      padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
    }
    .theme-card h4 { margin: 0 0 0.35rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
    .theme-card p { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.45; }
    .cites { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }
    .cites a { margin-right: 0.6rem; }
    .chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.35rem; margin: 0.5rem 0; }
    .chip {
      font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      background: var(--paper); padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 999px;
    }
  </style>

  <p class="note">
    Read the source:
    <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/eval/rancor/mcp_server.py`}>eval/rancor/mcp_server.py</a> ·
    <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/themes/islamophobia.yaml`}>themes/islamophobia.yaml</a>
  </p>
</Base>
